{
  "manufacturer": "Vaisala",
  "manufacturer_slug": "vaisala",
  "model": "DMT153 dew point transmitter (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "dmt153",
  "short_model": "DMT153",
  "aliases": [
    "DMT153",
    "DRYCAP DMT153"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (dew point transmitter)",
  "applies_to": "DMT153 trace-moisture dew point transmitter, Modbus RTU interface (user guide M213149EN-B).",
  "summary": "The DMT153 is a Vaisala DRYCAP transmitter for very dry gases (calibrated range -80 to -20 °C dew point) and the successor to the DMT152. In digital mode it is a Modbus RTU slave on RS-485. This map covers dew/frost point, ppbv and ppmw readings, status and error codes, pressure and molar-mass compensation, purge, analog outputs, limit alarms, test and user adjustment registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "DMT153 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M213149EN-B",
    "revision_date": "2026-06",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M213149EN-B/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 101-122 (Tables 15-27)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this and its worked read example confirms it.",
    "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
    "The 16-bit boolean output states 3594/3850 and the lock/unreliable flags 625/626 read 1 when active.",
    "Left out: device tag text (2561) and the calibration date/text block (8194-8228), which need multi-register text writes.",
    "Analog output clipping and error limits (1801-1807, 2057-2063) are left out.",
    "Calibration mode is turned on by writing 1300 to register 8193; the guide's adjustment procedures run in calibration mode.",
    "The four limit-alarm and analog-output parameter registers take the register address (hex) of the value to follow, as listed in the guide."
  ],
